⍝ Subtract.tc
⍝ ═══════════

⍝@ test4.

      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ Precond: A and B numeric
      ⍝ inv: A-B ←→ -(B-A)   (swapping operands negates the result,
      ⍝ even across int→float promotion)
      A ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      (A-B) ≡ -(B-A)
1

      ⍝ inv: A-B ←→ A+-B   (subtract = add the negation)
      (A-B) ≡ A+-B
1

      ⍝ Precond: Big sits at the int64 boundary so that Big-Small
      ⍝ always overflows and is promoted to float
      ⍝ (Cell::diff_overflow(), IntCell::bif_subtract_ii()); Small is
      ⍝ small enough to be exactly double-representable, so adding it
      ⍝ back to the float difference is exact
      ⍝ inv: Big ←→ (Big-Small)+Small
      Small ← ¯1-999∣|⎕RVAL 0     ⍝ negative: Big-Small overflows upward
      Big ← 9223372036854775807
      Big ≡ (Big-Small)+Small
1
      Small ← 1+999∣|⎕RVAL 0     ⍝ positive: Big-Small overflows downward
      Big ← ¯9223372036854775808
      Big ≡ (Big-Small)+Small
1
